1. The instant petition under Article 226 of the Constitution of India has been preferred seeking following reliefs:-
a) This Hon'ble Court be directed to the respondents to pay the compensation to the petitioner 10,000/- per year from 1996 till date, as loss damages occurred to the petitioner;
b) The respondents also be directed to release the land belonging to the petitioner from the encroachment and the part of the by-pass road which acrossed and constructed on the land which is useful for agricultural purpose be removed;
c) The respondent No.6 be directed to registered a criminal case under Section 420,
467, 468 of IPC against the respondent No.2 due to passing forged fabricated order in regard of exchange of land.
d) Other relief which this Hon'ble Court deems fit in the circumstances be granted and the cost of the petition be also awarded.
